WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.801
Neighbours and Society.

2
00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:06.433
Day 49 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.183 --> 00:00:09.207
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.487 --> 00:00:19.407
Today's goal: get to know your neighbours, ask for and offer help, handle complaints (noise, parking, leaks) politely, and speak up at a residents' association meeting.

5
00:00:20.757 --> 00:00:21.610
Part 1.

6
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:22.850
Key words.

7
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.444
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:40.871
Word or phrase, and Meaning. neighbour or next door or upstairs or downstairs: people near you. residents' welfare association (RWA) / society: building management group. secretary or committee or AGM:

9
00:00:41.151 --> 00:00:55.145
RWA roles or annual meeting. common area or clubhouse or lift or parking: shared spaces. maintenance charges: monthly fee for the building. complaint or request or notice: formal messages.

10
00:00:56.495 --> 00:00:57.370
Part 2.

11
00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:58.823
Friendly phrases.

12
00:01:00.073 --> 00:01:02.377
Hi, I'm Ashish from 304.

13
00:01:02.657 --> 00:01:03.831
We just moved in.

14
00:01:04.111 --> 00:01:06.180
If you ever need anything, just knock.

15
00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.487
Could I borrow a ladder for ten minutes?

16
00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.369
Could you collect my parcel if it comes while I'm out?

17
00:01:11.649 --> 00:01:13.975
We're having a small get-together on Saturday.

18
00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:15.449
Would you like to come?

19
00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:17.695
Part 3.

20
00:01:17.975 --> 00:01:20.301
Complaining politely: the 3 Fs.

21
00:01:21.551 --> 00:01:22.895
Here is a quick table:

22
00:01:23.175 --> 00:01:24.327
Rude, and Polite.

23
00:01:24.607 --> 00:01:26.036
Your music is too loud.

24
00:01:26.316 --> 00:01:27.169
Stop it.:

25
00:01:27.449 --> 00:01:28.132
Hi!

26
00:01:28.412 --> 00:01:29.649
Sorry to bother you.

27
00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:33.748
The music is quite loud in our flat, and my kids are trying to sleep.

28
00:01:34.028 --> 00:01:35.969
Could you turn it down a little after 10?

29
00:01:36.249 --> 00:01:37.657
Don't park in my spot.:

30
00:01:37.937 --> 00:01:41.372
Hi, I think your car is in my parking spot, number 12.

31
00:01:41.652 --> 00:01:43.380
Could you move it when you get a chance?

32
00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.647
Part 4.

33
00:01:45.927 --> 00:01:48.509
Conversation 1: noise from upstairs.

34
00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:51.785
Here is how the conversation goes.

35
00:01:52.065 --> 00:01:55.756
Hi, I'm Ashish from 304, just below you.

36
00:01:56.036 --> 00:01:57.636
Sorry to disturb you.

37
00:01:57.916 --> 00:01:58.897
Oh, hi!

38
00:01:59.177 --> 00:02:00.329
No problem.

39
00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:02.060
Is everything okay?

40
00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.513
Yes, mostly.

41
00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:09.041
It's just that we hear a lot of furniture moving late at night, around 11 or 12.

42
00:02:09.321 --> 00:02:10.559
Oh, I'm sorry!

43
00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:12.673
We've been rearranging the rooms.

44
00:02:12.953 --> 00:02:14.852
I didn't realise it was so loud.

45
00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.802
The conversation continues.

46
00:02:18.082 --> 00:02:19.149
No worries.

47
00:02:19.429 --> 00:02:22.117
My daughter has exams, so she sleeps early.

48
00:02:22.397 --> 00:02:24.103
Could you avoid it after 10?

49
00:02:24.383 --> 00:02:25.301
Of course.

50
00:02:25.581 --> 00:02:27.735
We'll put felt pads under the chairs too.

51
00:02:28.015 --> 00:02:29.509
That's really kind of you.

52
00:02:29.789 --> 00:02:30.706
Thank you!

53
00:02:30.986 --> 00:02:32.714
Thanks for telling us nicely.

54
00:02:34.064 --> 00:02:35.024
Part 5.

55
00:02:35.304 --> 00:02:38.269
Conversation 2: speaking at the society meeting.

56
00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:41.546
Here is how the conversation goes.

57
00:02:41.826 --> 00:02:43.661
Any other points from residents?

58
00:02:43.941 --> 00:02:46.821
Yes, I'd like to raise one point about parking.

59
00:02:47.101 --> 00:02:48.317
Please go ahead.

60
00:02:48.597 --> 00:02:53.354
Many visitors are parking in residents' spots, especially on weekends.

61
00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.066
Last Sunday, three of us couldn't park.

62
00:02:56.346 --> 00:02:57.605
That's true.

63
00:02:57.885 --> 00:02:59.314
It's happened to me too.

64
00:03:00.664 --> 00:03:02.264
The conversation continues.

65
00:03:02.544 --> 00:03:10.480
I'd like to suggest two things: visitor parking stickers, and the security guard asking visitors to use the visitor area.

66
00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.211
That sounds reasonable.

67
00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:14.624
Do we have a cost estimate for the stickers?

68
00:03:14.904 --> 00:03:15.928
I checked.

69
00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:19.579
It's about 2,000 rupeesfor 500 stickers.

70
00:03:19.859 --> 00:03:21.800
I'm happy to coordinate it.

71
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.019
Great.

72
00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:24.621
Let's vote on it.

73
00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.053
All in favour?

74
00:03:27.403 --> 00:03:28.342
Part 6.

75
00:03:28.622 --> 00:03:29.539
Practice.

76
00:03:30.789 --> 00:03:35.952
Write a polite WhatsApp message to your neighbour about their dog barking all day while they're at work.

77
00:03:37.302 --> 00:03:38.219
Success:

78
00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:39.587
Sample answer.

79
00:03:39.867 --> 00:03:41.382
Hi Neha, hope you're well!

80
00:03:41.662 --> 00:03:45.865
Just wanted to let you know that Bruno barks quite a lot during the day when you're out.

81
00:03:46.145 --> 00:03:48.897
I work from home and it's been hard during calls.

82
00:03:49.177 --> 00:03:52.718
Is there anything that might help, like a dog walker in the afternoon?

83
00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:54.065
Thanks so much!

84
00:03:55.415 --> 00:03:56.353
Part 7.

85
00:03:56.633 --> 00:03:57.679
Speak today.

86
00:03:58.929 --> 00:04:01.574
Greet a neighbour and ask one question about them.

87
00:04:01.854 --> 00:04:05.481
Practise one complaint using Friendly, then Fact, then Fix.

88
00:04:06.831 --> 00:04:08.367
That's the end of this lesson.

89
00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:13.297
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

90
00:04:13.577 --> 00:04:19.700
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

